"# aos-sweeper: one cleanup round for a daemon\n\nIt normally runs as the `_sweeper` loop row of each daemon (every 10 minutes in the templates). By hand, use `aos-daemon-ctl sweep` (`aos/cli/daemon.json#/sweep`) or:\n\n```sh\naos-sweeper -d stacks/root --dry-run --min-bytes 1000\n# _clock: would archive .../procs/_clock/stderr.txt (4053 bytes) to .../stderr_archives/2026-...Z.txt.gz\naos-sweeper -d stacks/root --report /tmp/rep.json     # also writes the round as JSON\n```\n\nOne round, only this daemon (child daemons are not entered): (1) stderr files of at least `--min-bytes` (default 1 MiB) are gzip-copied to `<stack>/stderr_archives/` and truncated to 0; (2) archives older than `--retention-days` (default 7; `none` = keep) are deleted; (3) only while the daemon runs, a loop in `D/procs/NAME/` that is off the table but proven alive gets a ctl stop, then SIGTERM `--stop-grace-s` (default 300) later; (4) old half-removed lock folders are deleted. History, ledgers and `.trash` are never touched. Another sweeper holding the lock = exit 0. Errors: `DaemonMissing`, `WriteFailed`.\n"
